(one connected contour pass - pre-finish or finishing - over a lathe polyline)
(the pass offset is produced by dynamic cutter compensation G41.1/G42.1 so)
(walls, tapers and radii all get a true normal-direction allowance: internal)
(fillets shrink and external radii grow by exactly the offset)
(optionally adds the loaded tool's nose diameter to the compensation)
o<lathe_poly_pass> sub
(CALL pds[1] shift_r[2] gx_base[3] gz_base[4] rot_total[5] pass_feed[6] li_len[7] li_ang[8] li_feed[9] lo_len[10] lo_ang[11] lo_feed[12] finish_mode[13] li_rad[14] lo_rad[15] nose_comp[16])

	#<pds>       = #1
	#<shift_r>   = #2
	#<pass_feed> = #6
	#<li_len>    = #7
	#<li_ang>    = #8
	#<li_feed>   = #9
	#<lo_len>    = #10
	#<lo_ang>    = #11
	#<lo_feed>   = #12
	#<li_rad>    = #14
	#<lo_rad>    = #15
	#<nose_on>   = #16
	o<lif_def> if [#<li_feed> LE 0]
		#<li_feed> = #<pass_feed>
	o<lif_def> endif
	o<lof_def> if [#<lo_feed> LE 0]
		#<lo_feed> = #<pass_feed>
	o<lof_def> endif

	(contour passes trace the full profile - no stock clamping, no early stop)
	#<_x_clamp_r> = 999999.0
	#<_trace_stop_rec> = 0

	#<rec_count> = #[#<pds>]
	#<entry_z>   = #[#<pds> + 1] (first record: lathe Z)
	#<entry_x>   = #[#<pds> + 2] (first record: lathe X radius)

	(pass travel direction: +1 = entered from the front, -1 = from the back)
	#<last_z> = #[#<pds> + [#<rec_count> - 1] * 8 + 1]
	o<zdir> if [#<entry_z> GE #<last_z>]
		#<z_dir> = 1
	o<zdir> else
		#<z_dir> = -1
	o<zdir> endif

	(normal offset via dynamic cutter comp: diameter and orientation come from)
	(the shared o<tip_comp_dia> so every lathe op derives nose comp identically)
	(- see lib/lathe/tip_comp_dia.ngc. comp_r is read back here, before comp is)
	(turned on, to place the raw lead-in on the already-compensated entry point)
	o<tip_comp_dia> CALL [#<shift_r>] [#<nose_on>]
	#<comp_d> = #<_tip_comp_d>
	#<comp_l> = #<_tip_comp_l>
	#<comp_r> = [#<comp_d> / 2]

	(entry direction, needed to place the already-compensated entry point below:)
	(the lead-in runs raw, before compensation turns on, so it must already land)
	(exactly where the comp'd contour actually starts - otherwise compensation)
	(establishes from an unshifted position and the first segment comes out at)
	(the wrong offset, and a tight blend radius trips the concave-corner check)
	(declared before the branch: a local first assigned inside one reads as)
	(not defined under load-time pre-parse, whichever way the branch goes)
	#<_2z> = [#<entry_z> - #<z_dir>]
	#<_2x> = #<entry_x>
	o<ent_dir> if [#<rec_count> GE 2]
		#<_2z> = #[#<pds> + 9]  (second record: lathe Z)
		#<_2x> = #[#<pds> + 10] (second record: lathe X radius)
		o<line> CALL [#<entry_z>] [#<entry_x>] [#<_2z>] [#<_2x>]
	o<ent_dir> else
		#<_line_cos> = [-#<z_dir>]
		#<_line_sin> = 0
	o<ent_dir> endif
	(offset side is above the contour: right of travel - 42 - entering from the)
	(front, left - 41 - entering from the back. The shared o<tip_comp_on> guards)
	(on a real diameter, so a nose-comp-off pass emits nothing. Resolved here,)
	(before the approach, because the arc-entry branch turns comp on itself)
	#<c_side> = 41
	o<c_sd> if [#<z_dir> GT 0]
		#<c_side> = 42
	o<c_sd> endif
	o<c_sd_id> if [#<_pl_side> EQ 1]
		(material is outside the profile on a bore, so the offset goes)
		(the other way - the inversion boring.ngc makes against taper.ngc)
		#<c_side> = [83 - #<c_side>]
	o<c_sd_id> endif

	(WHERE COMPENSATION ACTUALLY WANTS THE TOOL. This used to be the entry)
	(point plus comp_r along the plain normal to the first segment, which is)
	(not the rule the interpreter follows: with an L word the offset is)
	(ORIENTATION AWARE, and on a wall parallel to Z an orientation-2 tool sits)
	(on the surface with no radial shift at all. Landing 0.4 mm off it made)
	(the first cut the compensation entry move, and the wall came out tapered)
	(- r20.4000 at Z+1.0 falling to r20.0074 at Z-20.0 on testing_15_2, where)
	(the wall is programmed dead straight at r20.000. o<tip_comp_vec> is the)
	(same vector the parametric ops offset with, taken with the same side that)
	(o<tip_comp_on> is about to be given, so the two cannot disagree.)
	(control point = surface + r * normal - R * orientation. The ORIENTATION)
	(term arrives as two numbers from lathe_comp.orient_terms_gcode, so the)
	(nine-way table lives in Python and not in a hand transcription here. Only)
	(the normal is computed at run time, because it turns on the direction of)
	(the first segment of whichever record array this pass was handed - a)
	(runtime fact. Rotating a unit vector is arithmetic; the table is not.)
	(_line_cos/_line_sin are that unit direction, from the o<line> above.)
	(_tip_cam_r is the driver, not comp_r: it is the nose radius in BOTH native)
	(and In CAM mode and zero with compensation off, which is exactly the gate)
	(o<tip_comp_vec> applied. Guarding on comp_r instead would have left the)
	(orientation term applied to an already-offset In CAM path.)
	#<pe_dz> = [#<_2z> - #<entry_z>]
	#<pe_dx> = [#<_2x> - #<entry_x>]
	#<pe_len> = SQRT[[#<pe_dz> * #<pe_dz>] + [#<pe_dx> * #<pe_dx>]]
	(declared before the branch - a local first assigned inside one reads as)
	(not defined under load-time pre-parse, however the branch goes)
	#<pe_uz> = 0
	#<pe_ux> = 0
	#<pe_nz> = 0
	#<pe_nx> = 0
	#<comp_ez> = #<entry_z>
	#<comp_ex> = #<entry_x>
	o<pe_ok> if [[#<pe_len> GT 0.000001] AND [#<_tip_cam_r> GT 0.000001]]
		#<pe_uz> = [#<pe_dz> / #<pe_len>]
		#<pe_ux> = [#<pe_dx> / #<pe_len>]
		(measured against rs274, not derived: 42 gives u_x, -u_z and 41 gives -u_x, u_z)
		o<pe_sd> if [#<c_side> EQ 42]
			#<pe_nz> = #<pe_ux>
			#<pe_nx> = [-#<pe_uz>]
		o<pe_sd> else
			#<pe_nz> = [-#<pe_ux>]
			#<pe_nx> = #<pe_uz>
		o<pe_sd> endif
		#<comp_ez> = [#<entry_z> + [#<_tip_cam_r> * #<pe_nz>] - #<_pl_nose_oz>]
		#<comp_ex> = [#<entry_x> + [#<_tip_cam_r> * #<pe_nx>] - #<_pl_nose_ox>]
	o<pe_ok> endif

	(safe approach: retract above stock, rapid back in Z)
	o<ap_side> if [#<_pl_side> EQ 1]
		G0 X#<_pl_id_ret>
	o<ap_side> else
		G0 X[#<_wp_dia_od> + #<_x_clear> + #<shift_r> * #<_diameter_mode>]
	o<ap_side> endif

	(Does the contour trace begin on an ARC? The trace starts at record 2, so)
	(record 2 is the first move compensation sees - and an arc can neither)
	(establish compensation nor be programmed from the pre-shifted entry point,)
	(because its I/K are measured from wherever the machine actually is. Left)
	(alone this aborts the whole file with "Radius to end of arc differs from)
	(radius to start" by exactly comp_r. The arc branch below therefore runs the)
	(lead-in UNDER compensation and lands it on the raw entry point, making the)
	(straight lead-in itself the compensation entry move - which is what the)
	(rule actually asks for: a straight feed of at least the nose radius in)
	(free air. Everything downstream is then identical, and a straight record 2)
	(never enters this branch at all)
	#<comp_done> = 0

	#<arc_entry> = 0
	o<ae_chk> if [[#<rec_count> GE 2] AND [#<comp_r> GT 0.0001]]
		#<_r2_dir> = #[#<pds> + 11]
		o<ae_dir> if [[#<_r2_dir> EQ 2] OR [#<_r2_dir> EQ 3]]
			#<arc_entry> = 1
		o<ae_dir> endif
	o<ae_chk> endif

	o<lead_in> if [[[#<li_len> GT 0] OR [#<li_rad> GT 0]] AND [#<arc_entry> EQ 0]]
		(lead-in line direction: unit vector pointing from the entry toward)
		(the far rapid point - deliberately measured from the fixed Z axis)
		(here, NOT the local entry-segment direction _line_cos/_line_sin,)
		(unlike lead-out below. _line_cos/_line_sin at the entry points INTO)
		(the material about to be cut - the direction of the second record -)
		(continuing further in that same sense, as lead-out's fix correctly)
		(does for its own opposite-meaning, already-cut exit direction,)
		(pushes the far point and tangent point behind the entry - already)
		(inside the part - instead of safely in front of it. Verified)
		(numerically: for a front-face entry continuing into -Z, using the)
		(local direction placed the tangent point at Z<0, past the face,)
		(into the stock, with a 135 degree sweep; the Z-axis baseline used)
		(here places it at Z>0, safely in front, with the correct 45 degree)
		(sweep matching li_ang. 0 degrees continues along Z, 90 breaks radial)
		#<li_bz> = [#<z_dir> * COS[#<li_ang>]]
		#<li_bx> = [#<_pl_x_sgn> * SIN[#<li_ang>]]

		#<_flt_ok> = 0
		o<li_geom> if [#<li_rad> GT 0]
			o<fillet_lead> CALL [#<comp_ez>] [#<comp_ex>] [#<_line_cos>] [#<_line_sin>] [#<li_bz>] [#<li_bx>] [#<li_rad>] [#<z_dir>]
		o<li_geom> endif

		o<li_base> if [#<_flt_ok>]
			#<li_baz> = #<_flt_t1z>
			#<li_bax> = #<_flt_t1x>
		o<li_base> else
			#<li_baz> = #<comp_ez>
			#<li_bax> = #<comp_ex>
		o<li_base> endif

		G0 Z[#<li_baz> + #<li_len> * #<li_bz>]
		G0 X[[#<li_bax> + #<li_len> * #<li_bx>] * #<_diameter_mode>]
		(the lead feed applies to the STRAIGHT lead only - the blend radius is)
		(already cutting into the part at the contour's own direction, so it)
		(runs at the pass feed like the rest of the cut. With no lead feed set)
		(both resolve to the pass feed and the whole approach is one feed)
		F#<li_feed>
		o<li_str> if [#<li_len> GT 0]
			G1 X[#<li_bax> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<li_baz>
		o<li_str> endif
		o<li_fsw> if [#<li_feed> NE #<pass_feed>]
			F#<pass_feed>
		o<li_fsw> endif
		o<li_arc> if [#<_flt_ok>]
			(tangent blend from the lead-in line into the toolpath's own)
			(initial direction, instead of a sharp corner - run raw, before)
			(compensation turns on, so a tight blend never trips cutter comp's)
			(concave-corner gouge check, landing exactly on the already-)
			(compensated entry point)
			o<li_arc_d> if [#<_flt_cw>]
				G2 X[#<comp_ex> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<comp_ez> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<li_bax>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<li_baz>]
			o<li_arc_d> else
				G3 X[#<comp_ex> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<comp_ez> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<li_bax>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<li_baz>]
			o<li_arc_d> endif
		o<li_arc> endif
		F#<pass_feed>
		#<_cut_current_x> = #<entry_z>
	o<lead_in> elseif [#<arc_entry>]
		(the contour starts on an arc - approach along the lead-in line when)
		(there is one, straight down the Z clearance when there is not, and cut)
		(that approach with compensation already ON so it becomes the entry)
		(move. It lands on the RAW entry point: compensation applies the offset)
		(itself, instead of the pre-shift the straight-entry path above needs)
		o<ae_len> if [#<li_len> GT 0]
			#<ae_bz>  = [#<z_dir> * COS[#<li_ang>]]
			#<ae_bx>  = SIN[#<li_ang>]
			#<ae_dst> = #<li_len>
		o<ae_len> else
			#<ae_bz>  = #<z_dir>
			#<ae_bx>  = 0
			#<ae_dst> = #<_pl_z_clear>
		o<ae_len> endif
		(the entry move has to be at least the nose radius long or compensation)
		(refuses it - a short clearance must not be allowed to make it shorter)
		o<ae_min> if [#<ae_dst> LT [#<comp_r> * 2]]
			#<ae_dst> = [#<comp_r> * 2]
		o<ae_min> endif

		G0 Z[#<entry_z> + #<ae_dst> * #<ae_bz>]
		G0 X[[#<entry_x> + #<ae_dst> * #<ae_bx>] * #<_diameter_mode>]
		o<tip_comp_on> CALL [#<c_side>]
		#<comp_done> = 1
		F#<li_feed>
		G1 X[#<entry_x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<entry_z>
		F#<pass_feed>
		#<_cut_current_x> = #<entry_z>
	o<lead_in> else
		(plunge approach, landing on the already-compensated entry point)
		G0 Z[#<comp_ez> + #<z_dir> * #<_pl_z_clear>]
		G0 X[#<comp_ex> * #<_diameter_mode>]
		#<_cut_current_x> = [#<entry_z> + #<z_dir> * #<_pl_z_clear>]
	o<lead_in> endif
	#<_cut_current_y> = #<entry_x>
	#<_cut_phys_z> = #<entry_z>
	#<_cut_phys_x> = #<entry_x>

	o<co_1> if [#<comp_done> EQ 0]
		o<tip_comp_on> CALL [#<c_side>]
	o<co_1> endif

	(compensation now turns on right at the entry point instead of before the)
	(lead-in, so trace_lathe's own re-visit of record 1 - a zero-length move -)
	(would become the compensation entry move and fail the length check; start)
	(at record 2 instead, making the long record1-to-record2 cut the entry move)
	#<_pass_z_dir> = #<z_dir>
	o<trace_lathe> CALL [#<pds>] [0] [1] [0] [0] [0] [2]

	o<tip_comp_off> CALL

	o<lead_out> if [[#<lo_len> GT 0] OR [#<lo_rad> GT 0]]
		(the blend radius still leaves the part, so it stays at the pass feed;)
		(only the straight retreat below runs at the lead-out feed - see the)
		(matching note on the lead-in above. Both branches emit exactly one F,)
		(so with no lead feed set this is the same line the pass always emitted)
		o<lo_fsw> if [#<lo_feed> NE #<pass_feed>]
			F#<pass_feed>
		o<lo_fsw> else
			F#<lo_feed>
		o<lo_fsw> endif

		(g123_lathe only tracks the RAW programmed endpoint in _cut_phys_x/z,)
		(not where compensation actually left the tool - invisible when shift_r)
		(is zero on the finish pass, but wrong whenever the pass carries an)
		(offset: a facing-direction exit segment gets its offset applied in Z,)
		(not X, so the raw endpoint can be off by the full offset amount)
		o<ext_dir> if [#<rec_count> GE 2]
			#<_2z> = #[#<pds> + [#<rec_count> - 2] * 8 + 1]  (second-to-last record: lathe Z)
			#<_2x> = #[#<pds> + [#<rec_count> - 2] * 8 + 2]  (second-to-last record: lathe X radius)
			o<line> CALL [#<_2z>] [#<_2x>] [#<_cut_phys_z>] [#<_cut_phys_x>]
		o<ext_dir> else
			#<_line_cos> = [#<z_dir>]
			#<_line_sin> = 0
		o<ext_dir> endif
		#<_ext_nz> = [#<z_dir> * #<_line_sin>]
		#<_ext_nx> = [-#<z_dir> * #<_line_cos>]
		#<end_z>  = [#<_cut_phys_z> + #<comp_r> * #<_ext_nz>]
		#<phys_x> = [#<_cut_phys_x> + #<comp_r> * #<_ext_nx>]

		(the move right after exiting cutter comp must be straight, not an arc -)
		(a same-point no-op line satisfies that before a lead-out fillet blend)
		G1 X[#<phys_x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<end_z>

		(lead-out line direction: identical to the roughing lead-out in)
		(lathe_level_pass.ngc - retreat toward the pass start, +Z for a)
		(front-to-back pass, lifting +X, at the user angle - so every)
		(lead-out arc, roughing or finishing/pre-finishing, has the same)
		(geometric direction and dimensions. Measured from the Z axis, not)
		(the local exit segment: a roughing level always travels pure Z and)
		(retreats this way, and the user wants the finishing passes to match)
		(it exactly. 0 degrees continues along Z, 90 breaks fully radial)
		#<lo_bz> = [#<z_dir> * COS[#<lo_ang>]]
		#<lo_bx> = [#<_pl_x_sgn> * SIN[#<lo_ang>]]

		#<_flt_ok> = 0
		o<lo_geom> if [#<lo_rad> GT 0]
			(arrival direction: same as the one used to correct the exit point -)
			(the lead direction is negated because fillet_lead's T1 formula)
			(assumes travel INTO T1 along -lead; lead-out actually travels)
			(OUT of T1 along +lead, so the sense fed in must be reversed to)
			(place T1 where it is actually tangent to the real lo_str line)
			(cap the radius so the arc's own reach along the lead-out line)
			(never exceeds lo_len beyond the cut end - otherwise a large)
			(lo_rad keeps pushing the whole retreat further out with no)
			(bound; half-angle comes from the arrival vs lead-out directions)
			#<_lo_reff> = #<lo_rad>
			o<lo_cap> if [#<lo_len> GT 0]
				#<_lo_cos> = [-1 * [[#<_line_cos> * #<lo_bz>] + [#<_line_sin> * #<lo_bx>]]]
				#<_lo_sin> = ABS[[#<_line_sin> * #<lo_bz>] - [#<_line_cos> * #<lo_bx>]]
				#<_lo_rmax> = [#<lo_len> * #<_lo_sin> / [1 + #<_lo_cos>]]
				o<lo_cap2> if [#<_lo_reff> GT #<_lo_rmax>]
					#<_lo_reff> = #<_lo_rmax>
				o<lo_cap2> endif
			o<lo_cap> endif
			o<fillet_lead> CALL [#<end_z>] [#<phys_x>] [#<_line_cos>] [#<_line_sin>] [-#<lo_bz>] [-#<lo_bx>] [#<_lo_reff>] [#<z_dir>]
		o<lo_geom> endif

		o<lo_arc> if [#<_flt_ok>]
			(traversed V-to-T1, the reverse of how the utility defines the)
			(sweep, so the direction is flipped - verified numerically by)
			(checking actual tangent direction continuity at both ends, not)
			(just that the arc is a valid circle)
			o<lo_arc_d> if [#<_flt_cw>]
				G3 X[#<_flt_t1x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<_flt_t1z> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<phys_x>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<end_z>]
			o<lo_arc_d> else
				G2 X[#<_flt_t1x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<_flt_t1z> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<phys_x>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<end_z>]
			o<lo_arc_d> endif
			#<phys_x> = #<_flt_t1x>
			#<end_z>  = #<_flt_t1z>
		o<lo_arc> endif
		o<lo_str> if [#<lo_len> GT 0]
			o<lo_fsw2> if [#<lo_feed> NE #<pass_feed>]
				F#<lo_feed>
			o<lo_fsw2> endif
			G1 X[[#<phys_x> + #<lo_len> * #<lo_bx>] * #<_diameter_mode>] Z[#<end_z> + #<lo_len> * #<lo_bz>]
		o<lo_str> endif
		F#<pass_feed>
	o<lead_out> endif

o<lathe_poly_pass> endsub
